
// void has width 0 but still has to have an alignment of 1, or align_up
// would divide by zero.

// Raises n to `to` when it is below `lim`: an alignment of 1 for void, and a
// count of 7 for an int with no width, which are the two uses.
if_below(int n, int lim, int to) {
  int r = n;
  if(n < lim) {
    r = to;
  }
} return int r;
(4, 1, 1):(4)
(0, 1, 1):(1)
(5, 0, 7):(5)
(-1, 0, 7):(7)
